---
permalink: /quay/
title: Quay — Manage Local Dev Services from the macOS Menu Bar
description: Start, stop and monitor local dev servers, Homebrew services, Docker containers and terminal agents from one macOS menu bar app. Free and open source.
keywords: quay, macos menubar app, dev services manager, localhost ports, docker, homebrew
generate_social_image: false
image: /assets/img/quay/social-media-preview.png
---

{% extends "./_layouts/base.njk" %}
{% from "components/desktop-frame.njk" import desktopFrame %}

{% block custom_style %}
	{% set css_quay %}{% include "css/quay.css" %}{% endset %}
	{{ css_quay | cssmin | safe }}
{% endblock %}

{% set repo = "https://github.com/manustays/quay" %}
{% set download = "https://github.com/manustays/quay/releases/latest" %}

{% block main %}
<div class="quay">

	{# ---------- Hero ---------- #}
	<section class="block quay-hero">
		<div class="quay-hero-grid">
			<div class="quay-hero-copy">
				<div class="quay-hero-head">
					<img class="quay-logo" src="/assets/img/quay/logo.svg" alt="" width="88" height="88" />
					<div class="quay-hero-titles">
						<div class="quay-wordmark">Quay</div>
						<div class="quay-pronounce mono">/kiː/ · where your ports come in</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<h1 class="quay-headline">Your entire local dev stack.<br><span class="hl">One menu bar.</span></h1>

				<p class="quay-lede">Start, stop and monitor dev servers, Homebrew services, Docker containers and terminal agents from one lightweight macOS app — with live health, CPU and memory, and port-conflict detection.</p>

				<div class="quay-cta">
					<a class="button" href="{{ download }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
						{% svgico 'arrow-circle-down' %}Download for macOS
					</a>
					<a class="button secondary" href="{{ repo }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
						{% svgico 'github' %}View on GitHub
					</a>
				</div>

				<p class="quay-note">
					<svg class="quay-note-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><line x1="12" y1="11" x2="12" y2="16"/><circle cx="12" cy="8" r="0.6" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/></svg>
					Preview builds aren't notarized yet — macOS may ask for one confirmation in Privacy &amp; Security. Fully open source under MIT.
				</p>

				<ul class="quay-badges">
					<li>macOS</li>
					<li>Rust + TypeScript</li>
					<li>Tauri v2</li>
					<li>MIT</li>
				</ul>
			</div>

			<div class="quay-hero-visual">
				{{ desktopFrame("/assets/img/quay/popup.png", "Quay menubar popup listing running dev services with live status, CPU and memory metrics.", transparent=true) }}
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	{# ---------- Positioning callout ---------- #}
	<section class="block quay-callout quay-highlight-bg">
		<p class="quay-callout-text">
			<span class="quay-callout-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
			Not just a port monitor — <span class="hl">a control center for everything running locally.</span>
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="quay-highlight-bg">

	{# ---------- Four kinds of service ---------- #}
	<section class="block">
		<!-- p class="quay-eyebrow">Everything running locally</p -->
		<h2 class="quay-kinds-title">Four kinds of service. One place.</h2>
		<ul class="quay-kinds">
			<li class="quay-kind">
				<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'feature-services' %}</span>
				<h3>Project servers</h3>
				<p>Next.js, Vite, Django, Rails — auto-detected from your project config and grouped into one stack.</p>
			</li>
			<li class="quay-kind">
				<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'feature-brew' %}</span>
				<h3>Homebrew services</h3>
				<p>Redis, Postgres, MySQL, MongoDB. Start and stop brew services without touching the terminal.</p>
			</li>
			<li class="quay-kind">
				<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'feature-docker' %}</span>
				<h3>Docker containers</h3>
				<p>See and control running containers alongside everything else — no separate dashboard.</p>
			</li>
			<li class="quay-kind">
				<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'feature-terminal' %}</span>
				<h3>Terminal &amp; AI agents</h3>
				<p>Keep long-running processes like Claude Code visible, with uptime and resource use at a glance.</p>
			</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	{# ---------- Features ---------- #}
	<section class="block">
		<h2 class="quay-section-title">One dock for every local service</h2>
		<ul class="quay-features">
			<li class="quay-feature">
				<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'feature-services' %}</span>
				<h3>Unified management</h3>
				<p>Node &amp; Python servers, Homebrew services, Docker containers and terminal agents — all in one list.</p>
			</li>
			<li class="quay-feature">
				<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'feature-health' %}</span>
				<h3>Live status &amp; health</h3>
				<p>Process-liveness checks plus HTTP health verification so you know what's actually up.</p>
			</li>
			<li class="quay-feature">
				<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'feature-metrics' %}</span>
				<h3>Resource metrics</h3>
				<p>Real-time CPU and memory usage per service, right in the menubar.</p>
			</li>
			<li class="quay-feature">
				<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'feature-browser' %}</span>
				<h3>One-click browser</h3>
				<p>Open <code>localhost:&lt;port&gt;</code> for any running service without hunting for the port.</p>
			</li>
			<li class="quay-feature">
				<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'feature-radar' %}</span>
				<h3>Port radar</h3>
				<p>Detects unmanaged dev servers on your machine — adopt them into Quay or terminate them.</p>
			</li>
			<li class="quay-feature">
				<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'feature-stack' %}</span>
				<h3>Stack-aware</h3>
				<p>Recognises frameworks like Vite, Next, Django and Rails and shows the right tech-stack icon.</p>
			</li>
			<li class="quay-feature">
				<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'feature-favorites' %}</span>
				<h3>Organised your way</h3>
				<p>Favorites, search and collapsible groups keep a long list of services tidy.</p>
			</li>
			<li class="quay-feature">
				<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'feature-detect' %}</span>
				<h3>Auto-detection</h3>
				<p>Reads start commands and ports from <code>package.json</code>, <code>requirements.txt</code> and <code>.env</code>.</p>
			</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	</section>

	{# ---------- How it works ---------- #}
	<section class="block bg-shaded">
		<h2 class="quay-section-title">Up and running in a minute</h2>
		<ol class="quay-steps">
			<li class="quay-step">
				<h3>Install</h3>
				<p>Download the latest <code>.dmg</code> and drag Quay to <code>/Applications</code>.</p>
			</li>
			<li class="quay-step">
				<h3>Add a service</h3>
				<p>Hit <code>+ Add</code>, pick a project folder — Quay auto-fills the start command and port.</p>
			</li>
			<li class="quay-step">
				<h3>Control it</h3>
				<p>Start, stop, open in the browser or jump to a terminal — all from the menubar.</p>
			</li>
		</ol>
	</section>

	{# ---------- Build from source ---------- #}
	<section class="block quay-build">
		<h2 class="quay-section-title">Prefer to build it yourself?</h2>
		<pre class="quay-code mono"><span class="comment"># Requires Rust and Node — see the README for details</span>
git clone {{ repo }}.git
cd quay
npm install
npm run tauri build</pre>
	</section>

	{# ---------- Support / sponsor ---------- #}
	<section class="block quay-support">
		<div class="quay-support-card">
			<span class="quay-support-ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'heart' %}</span>
			<h2 class="quay-section-title quay-support-title">Enjoying Quay?</h2>
			<p class="quay-support-text">Quay is free and open source, built in my spare time. If it saves you time, a one-time sponsorship — or even a quick star — genuinely helps and keeps me motivated.</p>
			<div class="quay-cta quay-support-cta">
				<a class="button sponsor" href="https://github.com/sponsors/manustays?frequency=one-time" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
					{% svgico 'heart' %}Sponsor on GitHub
				</a>
				<a class="button secondary" href="{{ repo }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
					{% svgico 'github' %}Star on GitHub
				</a>
			</div>
			<p class="quay-support-note">No pressure — Quay stays free either way.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	{# ---------- Closing CTA ---------- #}
	<section class="block quay-closing">
		<div class="quay-cta">
			<a class="button" href="{{ download }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
				{% svgico 'arrow-circle-down' %}Download for macOS
			</a>
		</div>
		<p class="quay-license">MIT © 2026 Kumar Abhishek</p>
	</section>

</div>
{% endblock %}
